# Netlify caching rules for the live site.
#
# "must-revalidate" tells browsers to check with the server every time.
# If nothing has changed the server replies "still the same" (a tiny,
# fast response) and the browser reuses what it already has. If something
# HAS changed, the visitor gets the new version straight away.
#
# Without this, someone who visited last week could still see the old
# styling after we publish a change.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
